    "description": "If the reason you want a leaf vacuum is the mulch, the WG509 is the one to look at. Worx rates its two-stage all-metal mulching system at 18:1, meaning 18 bags of loose leaves reduce to roughly one. That is the highest mulch ratio of the handheld machines here, and the output is fine enough to spread straight onto beds or mix into a compost pile. Worx rates the motor at 12 amps and the blower at 350 CFM and 210 mph. The convenience feature that sets it apart is mode switching. Rather than unclipping one tube and fitting another, you flip a lever to go from blowing to vacuuming, which matters when you are clearing a bed edge and want to pull the pile straight into the bag. The 1.2-bushel bag is generous. With nearly 12,000 Amazon ratings it is also very well proven. Its Amazon average is a little below the Toro's, it is corded, and like every fine-shredding vacuum it works best on dry leaves. Use it on dry days and empty the bag before it is packed full."
